<newsitem itemid="175672" id="root" date="1996-11-08" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Unilever Q3 pretax rises.</title>
<headline>Unilever Q3 pretax rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter to end-September</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		26.98		  vs 26.03</p>
<p> Interim dividend(pence)10.29		  vs N/A</p>
<p> Pretax		     826		    vs 786</p>
<p> Turnover		   8,747		  vs 8,190</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on Q3 pre-tax profits were in a range of 760 to 820 million stg.</p>
<p>The company said the interim dividend was up 46 percent from the year-ago period.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 886		    vs 843</p>
<p> Interest payable	 66		     vs 73</p>
<p> Tax			  290		    vs 281</p>
<p> Net taxed		  505		    vs 485</p>
<p> Pay date		   Dec 20</p>
<p> Div registration date  Nov 26</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Nov 18</p>
<p>NOTE: Current Q3 includes 32 million stg net exceptional charges for restructuring projects in its recently-acquired industrial cleaning business, Diversey.</p>
<p>Net profit is at current exchange rates for each period.  </p>
<p>			 Nine months to end-September</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		63.48		  vs 63.98</p>
<p> Pretax		     1,951		  vs 1,906</p>
<p> Turnover		   25,240		 vs 23,433</p>
<p> Operating profit	 2,131		  vs 2,067</p>
<p> Interest payable	 198		    vs 190</p>
<p> Tax			  702		    vs 664</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1,189		  vs 1,193</p>
<p>NOTE: Nine months exceptional items included charges of 140 million stg in the current year versus a year-ago gain of eight million stg. Unilever Plc is an Anglo-Dutch consumer group.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
